        "id": 19341,
        "name": "Godai",
        "username": "Godai",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/godai/{size}/1920_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-07-26T20:08:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The one area of Hero Character Creation I find myself stumbling around is the decision that certain Principles are only&nbsp;available if you pick a certain Background or Archetype. For example, if you have a Military background, you should have an Ideals Principle. Why not an Expertise or Responsibilities Principle? The idea that choosing Option A also locks you into Option B seems to run counter to everything else about this game, with its free form Build It How You Want it mentality.</p>\n<p>Any issues of game balance that I am overlooking here?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:59.783Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
